  "shopping": [
    "<div class=\"shopping-workspace\"><h2>Worth it?</h2><p class=\"sub\">Check it against your wardrobe.</p><div class=\"shopping-options\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Possible purchase\"><button class=\"active\" data-purchase=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Jacket</button><button class=\"\" data-purchase=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Overshirt</button><button class=\"\" data-purchase=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Slip-ons</button></div><div class=\"shopping-body\"><div class=\"verdict-image purchase-photo\"><img src=\"assets/purchase-0.webp\" alt=\"Black bomber, photographed in store\" width=\"1122\" height=\"1402\"><span class=\"store-photo-label\">On the hanger</span></div><div class=\"shopping-answer\"><h3 class=\"verdict-word \">Skip it</h3><span class=\"match\">Good style match, already owned</span><h4>Black bomber</h4><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Why</strong>Yes, it fits your style. Short hem balances your longer torso, clean shape fits Japanese minimal, and black fits your cool, deep winter colours.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>What it adds</strong>No new wardrobe role.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Already covered by</strong>You already own a black bomber with this shape and colour, so this one would duplicate it.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Try instead</strong>Wear your black bomber instead of adding a second one.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Wear it with</strong>Your white heavyweight T-shirt and dark indigo straight jeans.</div></div></div><div class=\"shopping-bottom\"><p class=\"sub\">Sample wardrobe advice. No live photo analysis.</p></div></div>",
    "<div class=\"shopping-workspace\"><h2>Worth it?</h2><p class=\"sub\">Check it against your wardrobe.</p><div class=\"shopping-options\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Possible purchase\"><button class=\"\" data-purchase=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Jacket</button><button class=\"active\" data-purchase=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Overshirt</button><button class=\"\" data-purchase=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Slip-ons</button></div><div class=\"shopping-body\"><div class=\"verdict-image purchase-photo\"><img src=\"assets/purchase-1.webp\" alt=\"Olive cotton overshirt, photographed in store\" width=\"1122\" height=\"1402\"><span class=\"store-photo-label\">On the hanger</span></div><div class=\"shopping-answer\"><h3 class=\"verdict-word \">Skip it</h3><span class=\"match\">Good style match, already owned</span><h4>Olive cotton overshirt</h4><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Why</strong>The olive cotton overshirt works as an open layer over your white heavyweight tee, with slate pleated trousers and black leather loafers for Date night.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>What it adds</strong>No new wardrobe role.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Already covered by</strong>You already own this olive cotton overshirt and use it in Date night outfits. Another one would repeat that role.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Try instead</strong>Use the olive cotton overshirt you already own for Date night.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Wear it with</strong>Your white heavyweight T-shirt, slate pleated trousers and black leather loafers.</div></div></div><div class=\"shopping-bottom\"><p class=\"sub\">Sample wardrobe advice. No live photo analysis.</p></div></div>",
    "<div class=\"shopping-workspace\"><h2>Worth it?</h2><p class=\"sub\">Check it against your wardrobe.</p><div class=\"shopping-options\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Possible purchase\"><button class=\"\" data-purchase=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Jacket</button><button class=\"\" data-purchase=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Overshirt</button><button class=\"active\" data-purchase=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Slip-ons</button></div><div class=\"shopping-body\"><div class=\"verdict-image purchase-photo\"><img src=\"assets/purchase-light-canvas.png\" alt=\"Light grey canvas slip-ons, photographed in store\" width=\"1122\" height=\"1402\"><span class=\"store-photo-label\">On display</span></div><div class=\"shopping-answer\"><h3 class=\"verdict-word accent\">Worth trying on</h3><span class=\"match\">Good style match</span><h4>Light grey canvas slip-ons</h4><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Why</strong>A low-profile canvas slip-on suits your relaxed outfits. Light grey keeps the colour quiet, and the simple shape works with straight trousers or tailored shorts.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>What it adds</strong>A light canvas shoe you do not own. Your stone suede loafers cover a smarter finish; these add a breathable casual option.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Already covered by</strong>Your stone suede loafers cover a smarter finish; these canvas slip-ons serve a different, casual role.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Try instead</strong>Try your white leather sneakers first to see whether you need another light casual shoe.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Wear it with</strong>The ink navy heavyweight T-shirt and black tailored shorts, or your dark indigo straight jeans.</div><div class=\"detail\"><strong>Try-on check</strong>Walk a few steps: your heel should stay secure without rubbing, and the canvas should not press across your toes.</div></div></div><div class=\"shopping-bottom\"><p class=\"sub\">Sample wardrobe advice. No live photo analysis.</p></div></div>"
